rex — Runtime Executive for Agents  v1

Usage:
  rex                    open the board (TUI)
  rex <command> [flags]

Sessions:
  ls [flags]                     list sessions
  new [flags] -- <prompt>        start a session (-tool -model -cwd)
  attach <sel> [flags]           open a session (ctrl+] detaches)
  reply <sel> [flags] -- <text>  answer a session that needs input
  send <sel> [flags] -- <text>   send raw input (stdin when no text)
  wait <sel> [flags]             block until a session reaches a state
  rename <sel> <slug>            change a session's slug
  name <sel> [-clear] [-- <text>]
                                 set, show or clear the display name
  done <sel> [-after 72h]        mark done; cleared after retire_after_hours
  undone <sel>                   cancel a pending done
  archive <sel>                  archive a session
  resume <sel> [-print]          respawn an exited session (-print: only the
                                 resume id)
  complete <sel>                 stop a session now and mark it done
  rm <sel> [-force]              delete a session (-force without a terminal)
  prune [-dry-run] [-yes]        delete Completed sessions
  log <sel> [flags]              print a session's transcript (-f follows)

Daemon:
  status [flags]  session counts; exit 1 if one needs input
  daemon start|stop|restart|status|logs
                  manage the rex-daemon
  reload [flags]  reload tools.yaml in the daemon

Insights:
  digest [flags]           today's sessions, time and totals
  stats [flags]            lifetime usage by model and tool
  fleet ls|show|set|unset  list or edit session fleets

Lifecycle:
  setup [flags]      guided first-run wizard (-yes for defaults)
  doctor [flags]     check the install; exit 1 if a check fails
  update [flags]     upgrade rex in place (-check only looks)
  uninstall [flags]  remove rex and optional state

Other:
  config list|get|set|reset|edit  view and change settings
  render [flags]                  render an event stream from stdin
  completion bash|zsh|fish        print a shell completion script
  version                         print the version
  agent-help                      the usage card for LLM agents

Output:
